proof.text:
For the second normalization, expand $\beta_{20,K}$ and $a_{W_0K}$ and cancel the adjacent component inverses:
$$\beta_{20,K}a_{W_0K}d_{W_0K}
=W_2(\chi_{20,K})\alpha_{20,K}\chi_{20,W_0K}^{-1}\chi_{20,W_0K}\mu_{W_0K}d_{W_0K}^{-1}d_{W_0K}
=W_2(\chi_{20,K})\alpha_{20,K}\mu_{W_0K}.$$
For the other path, the first normalization and $a_Kd_K=\chi_{20,K}\mu_K$ give
$$W_2(a_K)\beta_{21,B_{10}K}B_{21}(\beta_{10,K})d_{W_0K}
=W_2(\chi_{20,K})W_2(\mu_K)\alpha_{21,T_{10}K}T_{21}(\alpha_{10,K}).$$
The assumed ordinary tower equation makes these two expressions equal. Cancel the invertible $d_{W_0K}$ on the right by composing with its inverse. This proves the transported tower equation by the category laws of [def-nagata-category].
